  <content>
  <section><para>Here is a graph of a function \(w\) defined by \(w(x)=(x+1.6)(x-2)\). Three points on the graph are labeled.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/74b2c12481cf4b589d93d52105cae863756c18dc"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Use the graph to answer the following questions.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="dcaecaca-551f-4428-b461-397612b1b26c"><problem><para>
      <para>Find the value of \(a\). Be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:<emphasis/></para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>-1.6</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is -1.6.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
